%description:

Tcp.maxPersistTimeout:invalid -- a value of 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "more than 0".

The classes: caps-growth (a value above the RTO; 60s is the default, 120s the value of
LinuxTcp): the interval of the probes starts at the RTO, doubles, and stops at the value;
caps-first (a value below the RTO): the first interval is the value too; invalid (0 and
less). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::startPersistTimer() and processPersistTimer(); the
check in TcpAlgorithm::initialize().

Host under test: host1, whose connection creates its algorithm at the open. Observation: the
error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.maxPersistTimeout
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.maxPersistTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpMaxPersistTimeoutInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.maxPersistTimeout = 0s    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
maxPersistTimeout must be more than 0, but it is 0 
